ui_rules.text:
- Which state covers a worker (U.S. Department of Labor, UIPL 20-04 of 10 May 2004, and Comparison of State UI Laws 2023, ch. 1), in this order:
- 1 the state where the service is localized: all of it is done there, or what is done elsewhere is incidental (temporary, transitory or isolated);
- 2 if not localized, the state of the base of operations, where some service is done;
- 3 the state the work is directed from;
- 4 only then the state of residence.
- A worker who lives in one state and works entirely in another is covered by the state of work.
- A worker who begins to telecommute from a new state is covered there from that date.
- Minnesota words its own test: see minnesota.
